1
00:00:47,777 --> 00:00:51,072
THE APARTMENT JOB

2
00:00:56,327 --> 00:00:59,164
Mr. Park, I'm sorry,
but I can't work here anymore.

3
00:01:00,165 --> 00:01:02,000
You can't just quit like this.

4
00:01:02,083 --> 00:01:03,960
You fired me suddenly too.

5
00:01:04,043 --> 00:01:06,546
You already received your payment.
You should do your job.

6
00:01:06,629 --> 00:01:08,756
What's the point in being your wife
for two more weeks?

7
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:12,051
You already got the position
that you wanted so badly.

8
00:01:13,052 --> 00:01:15,847
Our family still needs you, Ms. Kang.

9
00:01:15,930 --> 00:01:19,851
Mr. Park, that family you speak of
is fake anyway!

10
00:01:20,894 --> 00:01:21,728
What?

11
00:01:22,770 --> 00:01:23,771
"Fake"?

12
00:01:23,855 --> 00:01:25,732
Oh, my goodness. You…

13
00:01:27,066 --> 00:01:29,193
So you guys…

14
00:01:30,111 --> 00:01:31,613
were a fake family?

15
00:01:32,989 --> 00:01:34,282
I see.

16
00:01:34,365 --> 00:01:37,368
My gosh. I get it now.

17
00:01:37,452 --> 00:01:39,829
I did think it was strange.

18
00:01:39,913 --> 00:01:43,166
Those guys were telling their father
they'd cut off his hands,

19
00:01:43,249 --> 00:01:45,460
and you were telling the boy
to call you Ha-ri.

20
00:01:45,543 --> 00:01:48,171
I was wondering
what kind of messed-up family you were.

21
00:01:48,254 --> 00:01:50,006
So that's why.

22
00:01:50,757 --> 00:01:53,676
Everything was fake.

23
00:01:54,594 --> 00:01:55,595
Fake?

24
00:01:55,678 --> 00:01:56,971
You misheard.

25
00:01:58,431 --> 00:01:59,807
I said, "Take."

26
00:01:59,891 --> 00:02:02,852
I told her we needed to
take it easy on the salt.

27
00:02:04,562 --> 00:02:05,688
Right, honey.

28
00:02:05,772 --> 00:02:07,357
The kimchi stew was pretty salty.

29
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:09,192
-It was salty.
-Yeah, it was.

30
00:02:09,275 --> 00:02:10,526
It was salty.

31
00:02:10,610 --> 00:02:11,569
Enough about the stew.

32
00:02:11,653 --> 00:02:14,822
I heard it clearly with my own ears.

33
00:02:14,906 --> 00:02:17,450
"That family you speak of is fake anyway!"

34
00:02:17,533 --> 00:02:19,410
You misheard!

35
00:02:20,078 --> 00:02:21,079
That's nonsense.

36
00:02:21,162 --> 00:02:23,331
-Why would we fake a family?
-Right.

37
00:02:23,414 --> 00:02:24,707
Why would you do that?

38
00:02:24,791 --> 00:02:27,627
But you should know
that this is a serious matter.

39
00:02:27,710 --> 00:02:30,797
You've deceived
this entire apartment complex,

40
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:32,090
you understand?

41
00:02:32,173 --> 00:02:33,591
Ms. Jang, that's not--

42
00:02:33,675 --> 00:02:34,509
But…

43
00:02:35,301 --> 00:02:37,178
why did you go to such lengths

44
00:02:37,262 --> 00:02:39,222
to become the president?

45
00:02:39,305 --> 00:02:41,182
What are you scheming?

46
00:02:41,266 --> 00:02:42,558
What are you up to?

47
00:02:42,642 --> 00:02:43,977
-No, wait. Forget it.
-Ms. Jang…

48
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:46,104
President Park… I mean, Mr. Park.

49
00:02:46,187 --> 00:02:47,563
You…

50
00:02:48,147 --> 00:02:49,983
should step down immediately.

51
00:02:50,483 --> 00:02:54,028
I can't just let this slide.

52
00:02:54,112 --> 00:02:56,698
I'm going to post this
on our community forum.

53
00:02:56,781 --> 00:02:59,367
-Move aside.
-It's under maintenance.

54
00:02:59,450 --> 00:03:03,037
Darn it. This stupid elevator
is always out of order.

55
00:03:03,121 --> 00:03:04,664
You frauds.

56
00:03:05,331 --> 00:03:07,417
Ms. Jang…

57
00:03:22,015 --> 00:03:24,100
Emergency!

58
00:03:24,976 --> 00:03:27,186
Ms. Jang just found out
that we're a fake family.

59
00:03:27,270 --> 00:03:28,271
What?

60
00:03:30,064 --> 00:03:32,150
She just said
she's going to post this online.

61
00:03:32,233 --> 00:03:33,651
We have to stop her.

62
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:39,157
What's going on?

63
00:03:39,782 --> 00:03:43,328
Why isn't the internet working?

64
00:03:43,411 --> 00:03:45,788
What's wrong with this apartment?

65
00:03:45,872 --> 00:03:47,957
And why is the elevator

66
00:03:48,041 --> 00:03:49,584
stuck on the 29th floor?

67
00:03:52,879 --> 00:03:54,964
I can't hold on any longer.

68
00:03:57,884 --> 00:03:58,885
Gosh.

69
00:04:00,011 --> 00:04:01,429
What?

70
00:04:02,221 --> 00:04:03,681
I'm sorry, ma'am.

71
00:04:03,765 --> 00:04:05,767
It's not opening. Geez.

72
00:04:05,850 --> 00:04:06,851
What's going on?

73
00:04:07,602 --> 00:04:08,519
Darn it!

74
00:04:08,603 --> 00:04:10,229
This stupid apartment!

75
00:04:10,313 --> 00:04:12,482
I've had it with this place!

76
00:04:21,032 --> 00:04:23,951
It must smell nice
because it's from France.

77
00:04:24,911 --> 00:04:26,579
It's my first time using hand lotion.

78
00:04:27,163 --> 00:04:28,748
You didn't need to get me a gift.

79
00:04:29,332 --> 00:04:31,042
It's a farewell gift, Mr. Choi.

80
00:04:34,128 --> 00:04:36,964
You scare me whenever you say that.

81
00:04:37,048 --> 00:04:38,800
I told you several times.

82
00:04:38,883 --> 00:04:40,468
And President Seo

83
00:04:40,551 --> 00:04:43,596
also asked me to continue
just until the end of his term.

84
00:04:44,180 --> 00:04:46,599
So you returned when you heard
the president had changed?

85
00:04:47,475 --> 00:04:48,309
Yes.

86
00:04:50,395 --> 00:04:52,188
President Seo

87
00:04:52,271 --> 00:04:54,816
is in a tight spot
because he lost the election.

88
00:04:56,150 --> 00:04:59,445
None of us expected him
to lose that position.

89
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:02,323
I'll talk to him

90
00:05:03,032 --> 00:05:05,910
when the timing is right,

91
00:05:05,993 --> 00:05:07,912
so please stay until then.

92
00:05:07,995 --> 00:05:11,999
Without you here, our apartment complex
will be in huge trouble.

93
00:05:21,259 --> 00:05:22,176
Ha-jeong.

94
00:05:22,969 --> 00:05:24,512
It was a misunderstanding earlier.

95
00:05:24,595 --> 00:05:27,265
Our company's client asked me
to look after their son.

96
00:05:30,059 --> 00:05:33,312
Why would a lawyer
visit a client's house to do such work?

97
00:05:33,813 --> 00:05:35,481
And he called you "Mom."

98
00:05:36,566 --> 00:05:38,151
I had no choice. I'm just a newbie.

99
00:05:38,234 --> 00:05:39,735
I have to do as I'm told.

100
00:05:40,319 --> 00:05:42,530
And he loves me more than his mom.

101
00:05:42,613 --> 00:05:44,323
He just calls me "Mom" sometimes.

102
00:05:53,166 --> 00:05:55,209
You studied hard to become a lawyer.

103
00:05:55,293 --> 00:05:57,962
It upsets me
to see you running errands like that.

104
00:05:58,629 --> 00:06:00,381
Well, I told them I can't do it anymore.

105
00:06:01,799 --> 00:06:05,553
But why did you return so early?
Your trip was supposed to last longer.

106
00:06:07,388 --> 00:06:09,807
Something came up at work.

107
00:06:11,350 --> 00:06:14,395
You should've told me
so I could be prepared.

108
00:06:15,146 --> 00:06:16,105
Prepared for what?

109
00:06:18,816 --> 00:06:22,111
I mean, I would've picked you up
from the airport.

110
00:06:23,029 --> 00:06:24,822
Give me that. It must be heavy.

111
00:06:25,573 --> 00:06:26,616
How was France?

112
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:30,244
It was nice, but I did miss spicy food.

113
00:06:31,162 --> 00:06:35,124
That's a tacky way
to flaunt that you were abroad.

114
00:06:39,670 --> 00:06:40,838
You remember, right?

115
00:06:42,924 --> 00:06:45,259
First encounter, library
First kiss, under a street light

116
00:06:45,343 --> 00:06:46,886
Fateful encounter
At a book club after-party

117
00:06:48,763 --> 00:06:52,433
We checked that Ms. Jang went home
after struggling with the door last night.

118
00:06:52,516 --> 00:06:54,685
She'll come out
for her morning exercise soon.

119
00:06:54,769 --> 00:06:55,603
Okay, got it.

120
00:06:55,686 --> 00:06:59,565
Since it's an emergency,
I'll allow a wide range of touching.

121
00:07:03,527 --> 00:07:05,279
She's coming.

122
00:07:07,156 --> 00:07:08,282
Honey, hurry up.

123
00:07:09,492 --> 00:07:11,118
Careful not to get hurt, honey.

124
00:07:11,202 --> 00:07:13,621
You can protect me.

125
00:07:13,704 --> 00:07:15,706
I do protect you, don't I?

126
00:07:16,290 --> 00:07:17,375
-Shall we go?
-Yes.

127
00:07:17,959 --> 00:07:19,168
Gosh.

128
00:07:19,252 --> 00:07:21,003
I can tell that you're faking it.

129
00:07:21,087 --> 00:07:22,630
It's so obvious.

130
00:07:22,713 --> 00:07:24,715
Married couples
don't run around holding hands.

131
00:07:25,633 --> 00:07:27,718
Geez.

132
00:07:27,802 --> 00:07:29,637
We used to be in a book club.

133
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:32,348
I fell in love with her at first sight
at a library.

134
00:07:32,431 --> 00:07:33,891
Our first kiss was under a street light.

135
00:07:33,975 --> 00:07:35,142
Our first kiss…

136
00:07:35,226 --> 00:07:38,479
I don't want to know.
I'm not curious at all.

137
00:07:38,563 --> 00:07:40,690
I don't want to hear it!

138
00:07:41,357 --> 00:07:42,441
-Ms. Jang!
-Ms. Jang!

139
00:07:49,615 --> 00:07:50,533
One week.

140
00:07:51,158 --> 00:07:53,703
Can't you just wait one week?

141
00:07:55,788 --> 00:07:56,914
One week?

142
00:07:57,623 --> 00:08:00,543
What are you planning to do
during that week?

143
00:08:02,086 --> 00:08:05,381
Can't you give me a chance
to win back your trust?

144
00:08:10,177 --> 00:08:11,387
Don't you remember this place?

145
00:08:11,470 --> 00:08:13,139
Cut!

146
00:08:13,222 --> 00:08:14,682
That was soulless.

147
00:08:14,765 --> 00:08:16,142
Why is your tone so cold?

148
00:08:16,225 --> 00:08:18,644
You need to express more sincerity. Again!

149
00:08:19,604 --> 00:08:20,730
Sincerity.

150
00:08:22,023 --> 00:08:23,190
Do you remember this place?

151
00:08:23,774 --> 00:08:25,484
You and I stood here together

152
00:08:25,568 --> 00:08:28,404
and shouted ourselves hoarse
for a common goal.

153
00:08:28,988 --> 00:08:32,199
That glorious memory
of our struggle paying off

154
00:08:32,283 --> 00:08:34,702
is still engraved deep in my heart.

155
00:08:35,745 --> 00:08:36,954
All right, fine.

156
00:08:37,038 --> 00:08:38,831
That was a happy memory for me too.

157
00:08:38,914 --> 00:08:40,625
Our housing prices rose thanks to that.

158
00:08:40,708 --> 00:08:42,835
I do admire you for it.

159
00:08:42,918 --> 00:08:44,295
But you must have

160
00:08:44,378 --> 00:08:46,672
some reason to fake a family

161
00:08:46,756 --> 00:08:49,050
to become the president…

162
00:08:49,133 --> 00:08:50,301
…of the residents' association!

163
00:08:50,384 --> 00:08:52,511
I'm telling you, we're not a fake family.

164
00:08:52,595 --> 00:08:54,096
I really…

165
00:08:58,059 --> 00:08:59,101
love my wife.

166
00:09:00,394 --> 00:09:02,313
Sure, you do.

167
00:09:02,396 --> 00:09:04,023
You have to sincerely believe it

168
00:09:04,106 --> 00:09:07,026
when you say you love your wife. Again!

169
00:09:07,109 --> 00:09:07,985
Right.

170
00:09:08,694 --> 00:09:10,696
I really love my wife.

171
00:09:11,781 --> 00:09:12,698
I love her!

172
00:09:12,782 --> 00:09:14,075
I love her!

173
00:09:14,158 --> 00:09:15,660
I love her! With gestures too!

174
00:09:15,743 --> 00:09:17,244
-I love her!
-I love her!

175
00:09:17,328 --> 00:09:18,746
Gestures! I love her!

176
00:09:18,829 --> 00:09:22,166
I love her!

177
00:09:29,423 --> 00:09:31,092
I love my wife.

178
00:09:31,175 --> 00:09:33,886
I married her because I love her,
and we even had a child.

179
00:09:33,969 --> 00:09:36,263
I didn't want to tell you this,

180
00:09:36,347 --> 00:09:38,849
but my brothers
all have different mothers.

181
00:09:38,933 --> 00:09:41,185
Gosh. All three of them?

182
00:09:41,977 --> 00:09:45,022
My father had
a rather scandalous life in his youth.

183
00:09:45,106 --> 00:09:47,066
Right. I did think it was strange.

184
00:09:47,149 --> 00:09:51,404
You didn't look anything alike.

185
00:09:51,487 --> 00:09:52,863
What's more…

186
00:09:53,489 --> 00:09:55,658
my father started gambling, so…

187
00:09:55,741 --> 00:09:56,826
Oh, dear.

188
00:09:56,909 --> 00:09:58,452
We were so scarred because of him,

189
00:09:58,536 --> 00:10:02,415
but we were living together
to mend our relationship.

190
00:10:02,498 --> 00:10:05,710
Right. I see.

191
00:10:05,793 --> 00:10:07,378
-Oh, dear.
-Nice.

192
00:10:10,256 --> 00:10:12,174
Fine, let's say that's true.

193
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:13,968
However…

194
00:10:14,468 --> 00:10:17,888
from all the data I've collected so far,

195
00:10:17,972 --> 00:10:20,307
you guys are very suspicious.

196
00:10:20,391 --> 00:10:23,728
I have a bad feeling about you.

197
00:10:24,895 --> 00:10:28,941
That's why I'm asking you
to make your judgment after one week.

198
00:10:29,024 --> 00:10:31,527
It won't be too late to decide then.

199
00:10:37,533 --> 00:10:39,034
I didn't want to bring this up,

200
00:10:39,702 --> 00:10:43,247
but the maintenance fees
you're always complaining about…

201
00:10:46,250 --> 00:10:47,418
What?

202
00:10:47,501 --> 00:10:49,670
What about the maintenance fees?

203
00:10:51,046 --> 00:10:53,132
I think there's an issue with them.

204
00:10:53,215 --> 00:10:55,926
To be honest, I was investigating it.

205
00:10:56,802 --> 00:10:59,430
You were investigating that matter?

206
00:10:59,513 --> 00:11:01,223
You should've told me.

207
00:11:01,307 --> 00:11:02,892
So that's what you were doing.

208
00:11:06,604 --> 00:11:09,106
All right, fine.

209
00:11:10,649 --> 00:11:13,110
Then I'll give you just one week.
That's it.

210
00:11:13,611 --> 00:11:15,029
One week.

211
00:11:21,035 --> 00:11:24,079
THE APARTMENT JOB

212
00:11:24,872 --> 00:11:25,706
Boss.

213
00:11:26,874 --> 00:11:28,125
How did it go?

214
00:11:28,834 --> 00:11:31,420
We have one more week.

215
00:11:32,379 --> 00:11:34,840
We have to find the fund
within a week and flee.

216
00:11:36,050 --> 00:11:38,219
The Lizard. Bring him here.

217
00:11:38,302 --> 00:11:40,721
-Right.
-Lizard.

218
00:11:42,932 --> 00:11:44,600
I've been thinking about it.

219
00:11:45,351 --> 00:11:46,352
And?

220
00:11:46,435 --> 00:11:49,522
I've racked my brains,

221
00:11:50,147 --> 00:11:52,816
but let's say the facility manager,
the accounting manager,

222
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:55,694
and the president teamed up
and pocketed the fund.

223
00:11:55,778 --> 00:11:57,279
But even so,

224
00:11:57,363 --> 00:12:00,282
they wouldn't have emptied out
the entire account like this.

225
00:12:00,366 --> 00:12:03,077
You've been the president for a few days,
so you'd know.

226
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:07,540
Apartment complexes
have fixed monthly expenses,

227
00:12:07,623 --> 00:12:09,750
and unexpected emergency costs
come up all the time.

228
00:12:09,833 --> 00:12:11,585
Emptying out the entire account

229
00:12:11,669 --> 00:12:13,879
makes no sense.

230
00:12:13,963 --> 00:12:15,089
What's your point?

231
00:12:16,924 --> 00:12:20,135
There must be someone behind this.

232
00:12:20,928 --> 00:12:22,096
What?

233
00:12:22,179 --> 00:12:25,432
There are three major methods
to pocket the fund.

234
00:12:25,516 --> 00:12:27,726
First is to manipulate the books

235
00:12:27,810 --> 00:12:30,479
and skim off a little at a time.

236
00:12:30,563 --> 00:12:34,149
The second is to inflate
the construction costs, pay it out,

237
00:12:34,233 --> 00:12:36,068
then get a kickback from the contractor.

238
00:12:36,151 --> 00:12:39,238
Then the third is to just say,
"Screw it" and spend the money.

239
00:12:39,822 --> 00:12:41,156
Which method did you use?

240
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:45,244
I mixed all three methods, of course.

241
00:12:45,327 --> 00:12:47,079
Anyway, none of these methods

242
00:12:47,162 --> 00:12:49,540
would result
in an entirely empty bank account.

243
00:12:49,623 --> 00:12:52,751
Why? There can't be any problems
with emergency spending

244
00:12:52,835 --> 00:12:55,129
for you to pocket the money
without getting caught.

245
00:12:55,212 --> 00:12:58,507
That means someone powerful
is backing them.

246
00:12:59,592 --> 00:13:02,761
So there's someone behind the scenes
controlling the reserve fund?

247
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:05,723
Who?

248
00:13:08,684 --> 00:13:09,893
How would I know?

249
00:13:10,728 --> 00:13:12,146
-Bring the bag.
-It's in my closet.

250
00:13:12,229 --> 00:13:14,106
-Should we go up to the roof again?
-Wait.

251
00:13:14,189 --> 00:13:15,274
It might help you think.

252
00:13:15,357 --> 00:13:16,775
There's a way to find out.

253
00:13:21,697 --> 00:13:25,117
Use the fund with your position.

254
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:27,119
Whether it's construction or whatever,

255
00:13:27,202 --> 00:13:29,288
make something up
that requires you to use the fund.

256
00:13:29,371 --> 00:13:31,790
But if the construction proceeds

257
00:13:31,874 --> 00:13:33,917
when the account is empty,

258
00:13:34,001 --> 00:13:36,545
that means the money was paid

259
00:13:36,629 --> 00:13:39,048
and someone paid the contractor.

260
00:13:39,131 --> 00:13:42,801
It would cost quite a lot.
Will there be any issues using the fund?

261
00:13:42,885 --> 00:13:44,720
Not at all.

262
00:13:44,803 --> 00:13:46,889
This is exactly what
the reserve fund is for.

263
00:13:50,476 --> 00:13:51,602
We don't have time.

264
00:13:51,685 --> 00:13:54,938
Find anything that can be paid for
out of the reserve fund.

265
00:13:55,898 --> 00:13:56,815
-Yes, Boss!
-Yes, Boss!

266
00:13:59,526 --> 00:14:01,820
Don't let a single tile or nail
go unchecked.

267
00:14:01,904 --> 00:14:03,447
Check things that look fine too.

268
00:14:03,947 --> 00:14:05,240
Starting tomorrow,

269
00:14:05,324 --> 00:14:07,785
we're making sure this place
is under constant construction.

270
00:14:07,868 --> 00:14:09,536
-Let's find…
-Defects!

271
00:14:13,332 --> 00:14:14,291
Let's find some…

272
00:14:14,375 --> 00:14:16,543
The drains are way too open.

273
00:14:17,169 --> 00:14:18,587
They need to be open!

274
00:14:21,465 --> 00:14:22,675
Over here.

275
00:14:22,758 --> 00:14:24,551
We can do crack repairs here.

276
00:14:24,635 --> 00:14:26,470
See? I told you there were a lot.

277
00:14:27,262 --> 00:14:29,014
-There's one here!
-There's one here too!

278
00:14:30,140 --> 00:14:31,475
I found one here too.

279
00:14:33,852 --> 00:14:34,812
That's a selfie.

280
00:14:40,859 --> 00:14:41,819
It's leaking!

281
00:14:47,282 --> 00:14:48,325
A leak repair.

282
00:15:00,129 --> 00:15:02,631
Lizard, this one's a different color.
What's with this?

283
00:15:02,715 --> 00:15:04,216
It's the design.

284
00:15:05,217 --> 00:15:07,720
-What is it?
-I just tripped on a block. Right here.

285
00:15:09,054 --> 00:15:10,305
Hello.

286
00:15:10,389 --> 00:15:12,933
The new president is working really hard.

287
00:15:13,017 --> 00:15:14,226
Yeah, I'm glad he got elected.

288
00:15:14,309 --> 00:15:16,603
-Yeah. He's doing a great job.
-He is.

289
00:15:20,524 --> 00:15:21,775
Why is he working so hard?

290
00:15:25,696 --> 00:15:26,780
Great job, everyone.

291
00:15:26,864 --> 00:15:28,365
Let's enjoy our lunch.

292
00:15:28,449 --> 00:15:29,324
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

293
00:15:29,408 --> 00:15:31,368
You put all of these in?

294
00:15:31,452 --> 00:15:32,870
How do you make a profit?

295
00:15:32,953 --> 00:15:36,290
I want an Italian BMT sandwich
on grain bread,

296
00:15:36,373 --> 00:15:38,042
creamy egg salad with extra avocado,

297
00:15:38,125 --> 00:15:39,543
meat, pepperoni, and cheese.

298
00:15:39,626 --> 00:15:41,211
For the sauce, sweet low-sugar onion,

299
00:15:41,295 --> 00:15:43,255
tangy red wine vinegar
and a sprinkle of salt.

300
00:15:44,256 --> 00:15:46,258
-What will you have?
-Just have one.

301
00:15:46,341 --> 00:15:47,718
It's one sandwich.

302
00:15:47,801 --> 00:15:48,761
Really?

303
00:15:48,844 --> 00:15:51,305
I want one with meat.

304
00:15:51,388 --> 00:15:53,265
Stop. We'll all order the same one.

305
00:15:53,974 --> 00:15:55,851
Steak and cheese, please.

306
00:15:59,063 --> 00:16:00,814
This is really tasty.

307
00:16:00,898 --> 00:16:02,399
What is this? It's so good.

308
00:16:02,483 --> 00:16:04,860
This will keep me full until dinner.

309
00:16:04,943 --> 00:16:07,613
This is perfect for a man my age too.

310
00:16:08,322 --> 00:16:11,867
We did find things
to spend the reserve fund on,

311
00:16:11,950 --> 00:16:13,702
but what do we do now, Mr. Park?

312
00:16:13,786 --> 00:16:15,204
We need to move.

313
00:16:15,287 --> 00:16:16,121
FACILITY MANAGER

314
00:16:19,333 --> 00:16:21,960
Mr. Choi, we need
a building rep meeting immediately.

315
00:16:22,711 --> 00:16:24,671
Our apartment complex is a mess.

316
00:16:25,339 --> 00:16:27,800
Let's tackle the issues one by one.

317
00:16:27,883 --> 00:16:29,802
EMERGENCY MEETING
ORGANIZER: PARK HAE-KANG

318
00:16:38,977 --> 00:16:40,104
All right.

319
00:16:43,273 --> 00:16:44,441
Hello.

320
00:16:44,525 --> 00:16:46,902
I'm President Park Hae-kang of True Value.

321
00:16:53,325 --> 00:16:55,786
I called this emergency meeting today

322
00:16:55,869 --> 00:16:58,413
because there are several
urgent matters to address.

323
00:16:58,497 --> 00:17:01,083
It's been about six years
since residents moved in,

324
00:17:01,166 --> 00:17:03,669
so we're starting to see problems
popping up here and there.

325
00:17:03,752 --> 00:17:04,920
So first,

326
00:17:05,003 --> 00:17:08,632
I'd like to repair
the cracks in the parking lot.

327
00:17:08,715 --> 00:17:12,010
This must be done
with the long-term repair reserve fund.

328
00:17:12,928 --> 00:17:14,429
Excuse me.

329
00:17:14,513 --> 00:17:16,849
The parking lot floor is completely fine.

330
00:17:17,641 --> 00:17:20,394
You might not know
since you're new to the job,

331
00:17:20,477 --> 00:17:23,689
but you can't just use the fund
recklessly like that.

332
00:17:25,149 --> 00:17:26,984
I'm not suggesting we use it recklessly.

333
00:17:27,067 --> 00:17:29,153
I've been told we can use
the reserve fund for this

334
00:17:29,236 --> 00:17:31,697
since it's for facility replacement
and repairs.

335
00:17:31,780 --> 00:17:33,699
Just because it's possible

336
00:17:33,782 --> 00:17:37,369
doesn't mean this repair is necessary.

337
00:17:37,452 --> 00:17:38,912
Are you saying

338
00:17:38,996 --> 00:17:42,749
that we can just tear apart
or replace things that are perfectly fine

339
00:17:42,833 --> 00:17:44,877
as long as the fund covers it?

340
00:17:46,086 --> 00:17:48,338
I checked the apartment complex
here and there,

341
00:17:48,422 --> 00:17:50,132
and it wasn't perfectly fine.

342
00:17:50,215 --> 00:17:52,176
There are chips and scrapes everywhere.

343
00:17:52,259 --> 00:17:53,886
Construction is absolutely necessary.

344
00:17:55,137 --> 00:17:57,181
We should hold off as long as we can.

345
00:17:57,264 --> 00:17:59,474
You shouldn't waste
the reserve fund like this.

346
00:17:59,558 --> 00:18:00,559
Waste?

347
00:18:00,642 --> 00:18:03,187
It's his first time as president.

348
00:18:03,270 --> 00:18:05,939
He's just clueless about his job.

349
00:18:08,150 --> 00:18:10,903
Then let's put this to a vote.

350
00:18:10,986 --> 00:18:14,531
Who here agrees to repairing the cracks

351
00:18:14,615 --> 00:18:15,699
in the parking lot?

352
00:18:22,414 --> 00:18:24,208
All right. Those who oppose?

353
00:18:29,463 --> 00:18:31,048
The second item on the agenda

354
00:18:31,131 --> 00:18:33,300
is repairing the leak in the machine room.

355
00:18:33,383 --> 00:18:36,053
Who agrees to using the reserve fund?

356
00:18:36,845 --> 00:18:37,804
Who opposes?

357
00:18:38,555 --> 00:18:41,391
What? Everyone's opposing.

358
00:18:41,475 --> 00:18:44,228
And replacing the pavement blocks.

359
00:18:44,311 --> 00:18:45,145
Who here opposes?

360
00:18:46,772 --> 00:18:48,857
Why isn't he asking who agrees?

361
00:18:48,941 --> 00:18:50,567
Because it's too obvious.

362
00:18:51,944 --> 00:18:55,072
I knew it. I told you this would happen.

363
00:18:55,155 --> 00:18:56,406
Fourth item on the agenda.

364
00:18:56,490 --> 00:18:59,326
Who here opposes
repainting the buildings' exterior?

365
00:19:01,787 --> 00:19:06,041
Next, replacing the tiles and fixing
the floor in the community center.

366
00:19:06,124 --> 00:19:07,042
Who here opposes?

367
00:19:07,626 --> 00:19:11,213
Replacing the automatic
fire detection system.

368
00:19:11,296 --> 00:19:12,256
Who opposes?

369
00:19:13,173 --> 00:19:15,926
All right. Thank you, everyone.

370
00:19:16,677 --> 00:19:20,514
Why is everyone opposed
to what Uncle says?

371
00:19:21,098 --> 00:19:23,976
Uncle Hae-kang doesn't have
his own connections there.

372
00:19:24,059 --> 00:19:25,519
That's how harsh the world is.

373
00:19:25,602 --> 00:19:27,104
People take sides

374
00:19:27,187 --> 00:19:29,690
and want their team to win
while the other loses.

375
00:19:30,315 --> 00:19:31,733
This is bad for your education.

376
00:19:32,401 --> 00:19:35,445
Then we'll wrap up True Value's
building representative meeting.

377
00:19:35,529 --> 00:19:36,363
Thank you.

378
00:19:44,663 --> 00:19:46,331
Seo Gang-won is doing a good job.

379
00:19:46,999 --> 00:19:47,833
Everyone opposed.

380
00:19:48,417 --> 00:19:52,129
Our new president
is bold enough to plant relics.

381
00:19:52,212 --> 00:19:53,922
What will he do now?

382
00:19:54,006 --> 00:19:56,174
I'm pretty sure he won't just sit back.

383
00:19:56,258 --> 00:19:57,092
Sir.

384
00:19:57,175 --> 00:19:59,803
We got a call from the head of Hansu Bank.

385
00:19:59,886 --> 00:20:00,846
Why?

386
00:20:01,346 --> 00:20:03,598
True Value's
residents' association president

387
00:20:03,682 --> 00:20:06,768
came to withdraw the entire reserve fund.

388
00:20:08,603 --> 00:20:09,730
What?

389
00:20:09,813 --> 00:20:12,816
He would've found out
that the account is empty.

390
00:20:30,292 --> 00:20:31,209
Mr. Kim.

391
00:20:32,044 --> 00:20:33,170
I get it now.

392
00:20:33,670 --> 00:20:35,964
I get why Park Hae-kang
wanted to become the president.

393
00:20:36,548 --> 00:20:37,841
What's the reason?

394
00:20:39,509 --> 00:20:41,261
The reserve fund.

395
00:20:41,345 --> 00:20:44,222
He became the president
to pocket the fund.

396
00:20:44,306 --> 00:20:47,142
I never imagined that would be the reason.

397
00:20:47,809 --> 00:20:51,480
He found out it was empty,
so he's trying to use the fund.

398
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:55,317
I'm so excited right now.

399
00:20:55,400 --> 00:20:57,319
I'm going to lose my mind.

400
00:20:57,402 --> 00:20:59,446
I'm getting a dopamine rush!

401
00:21:06,036 --> 00:21:07,662
What's with those building reps?

402
00:21:07,746 --> 00:21:09,748
Why are they opposing everything?

403
00:21:10,707 --> 00:21:14,211
I feel like they're not helping
with the association's matters at all.

404
00:21:15,629 --> 00:21:18,215
Don't I have the authority to remove them?

405
00:21:18,298 --> 00:21:21,093
The building reps
are elected by the residents,

406
00:21:21,176 --> 00:21:24,221
so unless they're accused of corruption,
you can't dismiss them.

407
00:21:24,304 --> 00:21:26,515
They're standing in the way
of improving this place.

408
00:21:26,598 --> 00:21:28,016
That's basically corruption.

409
00:21:30,394 --> 00:21:31,228
Sir.

410
00:21:32,104 --> 00:21:33,230
Over there.

411
00:21:33,897 --> 00:21:35,524
She's our accounting manager.

412
00:21:38,902 --> 00:21:41,238
Let's say the facility manager,
the accounting manager

413
00:21:41,321 --> 00:21:44,449
and the president teamed up
and pocketed the fund.

414
00:21:44,533 --> 00:21:46,034
But even so,

415
00:21:46,118 --> 00:21:48,954
they wouldn't have emptied out
the entire account like this.

416
00:21:49,788 --> 00:21:51,123
The accounting manager.

417
00:21:51,206 --> 00:21:53,333
You didn't get to meet
since she was on vacation.

418
00:21:53,417 --> 00:21:55,502
Ha-jeong, this is the president.

419
00:21:59,548 --> 00:22:01,716
I've been wanting to meet you.

420
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:04,136
Hello. I'm Kang Ha-jeong.

421
00:22:04,219 --> 00:22:07,097
I'm Park Hae-kang. Nice to meet you.

422
00:22:07,681 --> 00:22:08,849
Nice to meet you too.

423
00:22:10,851 --> 00:22:13,937
We'll have a lot
to discuss together from now on.

424
00:22:15,230 --> 00:22:16,440
We will?

425
00:22:17,065 --> 00:22:18,483
We can talk next time.

426
00:22:19,443 --> 00:22:20,986
I'm heading out.

427
00:22:26,616 --> 00:22:28,785
I guess our apartment complex
is changing now.

428
00:22:28,869 --> 00:22:31,037
A man who lives alone
became the president.

429
00:22:31,997 --> 00:22:33,582
He doesn't live alone.

430
00:22:34,583 --> 00:22:36,501
He has a huge family.

431
00:22:41,214 --> 00:22:42,340
Do you live alone?

432
00:22:43,133 --> 00:22:45,760
Why? Is there a problem with that?

433
00:22:47,512 --> 00:22:49,055
Was it a different guy?

434
00:22:51,808 --> 00:22:55,437
Park Hae-kang will have no choice
but to step down.

435
00:22:55,520 --> 00:22:57,689
He would have realized today

436
00:22:57,772 --> 00:22:59,733
-that he can't do whatever he wants.
-Exactly.

437
00:22:59,816 --> 00:23:03,320
He must've been feeling pretty high
and mighty about becoming the president.

438
00:23:03,403 --> 00:23:04,487
-It's so satisfying.
-Totally.

439
00:23:04,571 --> 00:23:08,617
He'll learn
that popularity doesn't mean much.

440
00:23:08,700 --> 00:23:12,037
Once Park Hae-kang steps down,
you should return to your position.

441
00:23:12,120 --> 00:23:13,121
Absolutely.

442
00:23:17,209 --> 00:23:20,587
I think that's the thing about the world.

443
00:23:23,173 --> 00:23:24,925
This is nice and sweet.

444
00:23:26,384 --> 00:23:27,928
Things tend to follow…

445
00:23:29,763 --> 00:23:32,182
their natural course.

446
00:23:32,265 --> 00:23:33,683
Of course.

447
00:23:35,644 --> 00:23:37,729
Why are they against
using the reserve fund?

448
00:23:37,812 --> 00:23:39,648
Calm down, Mr. Park.

449
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:44,569
I'd have to be crazy
to be lying to you in this situation.

450
00:23:44,653 --> 00:23:47,239
You're giving me food, shelter
and clothes right now.

451
00:23:47,322 --> 00:23:49,491
-So?
-Gosh.

452
00:23:50,075 --> 00:23:51,743
You saw earlier

453
00:23:51,826 --> 00:23:54,704
how President Seo's supporters
are still groveling.

454
00:23:54,788 --> 00:23:59,251
That means President Seo
is still handing out kickbacks.

455
00:23:59,334 --> 00:24:00,961
-Kickbacks?
-Yeah.

456
00:24:01,044 --> 00:24:03,797
Even after Mr. Park became the president,

457
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:07,092
those assholes
are still clinging to President Seo

458
00:24:07,175 --> 00:24:08,927
and sucking up to him.

459
00:24:09,010 --> 00:24:10,262
Why would they do that?

460
00:24:10,929 --> 00:24:14,641
Because there's still
something in it for them.

461
00:24:14,724 --> 00:24:16,559
If I ask you what that is,

462
00:24:16,643 --> 00:24:18,937
you'll just tell me
to figure it out myself.

463
00:24:21,982 --> 00:24:22,983
How did you know?

464
00:24:24,317 --> 00:24:25,819
Wanna sleep in that bag again?

465
00:24:28,154 --> 00:24:30,824
How long will you threaten me with this?

466
00:24:30,907 --> 00:24:32,075
Isn't there anything new?

467
00:24:32,158 --> 00:24:33,451
Don't take it out on me.

468
00:24:33,535 --> 00:24:35,787
You should be dealing with
President Seo's bootlickers.

469
00:24:35,870 --> 00:24:38,915
You guys look into the building reps
supporting President Seo.

470
00:24:39,582 --> 00:24:40,792
We don't have much time.

471
00:24:40,875 --> 00:24:44,546
We have to find whatever we can
and get rid of them to use the fund

472
00:24:44,629 --> 00:24:46,298
and find where it went.

473
00:24:46,381 --> 00:24:49,551
President Seo and those bootlickers…

474
00:24:49,634 --> 00:24:51,594
I'll crush them to pieces.

475
00:24:56,558 --> 00:24:58,977
Did you forget the basics
of digging into people?

476
00:25:10,405 --> 00:25:11,906
Yes, I'm heading out.

477
00:25:12,741 --> 00:25:14,784
The font is so small.

478
00:25:28,006 --> 00:25:31,259
Hey, look at the bills.
Why are you looking at food?

479
00:25:31,343 --> 00:25:33,261
I can't find anything noteworthy.

480
00:25:33,345 --> 00:25:34,971
Maybe we've lost our touch.

481
00:25:35,055 --> 00:25:36,306
I'll look through them again.

482
00:25:37,057 --> 00:25:40,268
We can't use the reserve fund
while President Seo still holds power.

483
00:25:41,561 --> 00:25:43,146
We have to take them out first.

484
00:25:46,816 --> 00:25:48,276
I'm here.

485
00:25:53,948 --> 00:25:55,742
What is all this?

486
00:25:57,994 --> 00:26:00,121
Why do you have other people's bills here?

487
00:26:05,251 --> 00:26:07,128
Why is their heating bill zero?

488
00:26:10,215 --> 00:26:11,341
This one's zero too.

489
00:26:12,384 --> 00:26:13,343
And this one?

490
00:26:13,426 --> 00:26:17,514
Wait. How can all of them be zero?

491
00:26:18,056 --> 00:26:19,140
What is it?

492
00:26:19,224 --> 00:26:20,934
What's with these houses?

493
00:26:21,017 --> 00:26:23,353
-Their heating bills are zero.
-What?

494
00:26:25,772 --> 00:26:27,899
What is it? Let me see.

495
00:26:29,442 --> 00:26:31,653
That can't be possible.

496
00:26:33,696 --> 00:26:35,156
Does this make any sense?

497
00:26:35,240 --> 00:26:36,616
Over 100 households?

498
00:26:36,699 --> 00:26:39,160
Precisely 123 households
have a heating bill of zero.

499
00:26:39,244 --> 00:26:42,580
We've checked that they're paying
for their water bills and parking,

500
00:26:42,664 --> 00:26:45,166
but it's just the heating bill
that's zero.

501
00:26:45,250 --> 00:26:47,210
These are the households
with zero heating bills.

502
00:26:47,293 --> 00:26:49,796
They're the building representatives,

503
00:26:49,879 --> 00:26:51,965
including President Seo's
closest supporters.

504
00:26:52,048 --> 00:26:56,302
There are even
former building representatives.

505
00:26:56,386 --> 00:26:58,763
Ever since President Seo
formed the association,

506
00:26:58,847 --> 00:27:02,350
he's been the president all these years.

507
00:27:03,184 --> 00:27:05,687
So all of his supporters
have zero heating bills.

508
00:27:05,770 --> 00:27:06,896
That's right.

509
00:27:06,980 --> 00:27:10,191
The accounts that wrote
malicious comments about you

510
00:27:10,275 --> 00:27:12,569
are the same as those
that have zero heating bills.

511
00:27:12,652 --> 00:27:14,404
So he even ran a troll farm.

512
00:27:15,155 --> 00:27:18,575
These guys have obviously
been doing this for a long time.

513
00:27:18,658 --> 00:27:21,786
He formed the association
about six years ago, didn't he?

514
00:27:22,787 --> 00:27:25,540
Then they could've paid
zero heating bills for six years.

515
00:27:26,332 --> 00:27:28,293
So he gave them kickbacks through this.

516
00:27:29,002 --> 00:27:32,589
But if 123 households
haven't been paying their heating fees,

517
00:27:32,672 --> 00:27:35,300
then who was paying for them?

518
00:27:35,383 --> 00:27:36,468
The other 9,000…

519
00:27:36,551 --> 00:27:40,680
So the other 9,677 households
were paying for theirs.

520
00:27:40,763 --> 00:27:41,598
That's right.

521
00:27:41,681 --> 00:27:45,059
But they won't even know
that they're paying for them.

522
00:27:45,143 --> 00:27:46,853
This is just ridiculous.

523
00:27:46,936 --> 00:27:48,938
No one found out about this for six years?

524
00:27:49,022 --> 00:27:50,732
Shouldn't we report this to the media?

525
00:27:51,316 --> 00:27:52,525
Report this?

526
00:27:53,735 --> 00:27:55,236
Yes, that's right.

527
00:27:55,320 --> 00:27:57,780
We can make them step down
as building representatives

528
00:27:57,864 --> 00:27:59,073
if we make this public.

529
00:27:59,157 --> 00:28:01,784
Right! Your brain works well
in situations like this.

530
00:28:01,868 --> 00:28:05,788
Then you could eliminate everyone
who's against you all at once.

531
00:28:07,457 --> 00:28:08,291
Yes.

532
00:28:08,374 --> 00:28:11,503
Then will you become
another Heating Bill Martyr?

533
00:28:12,378 --> 00:28:13,254
What?

534
00:28:13,338 --> 00:28:15,089
Don't you know the Heating Bill Martyr?

535
00:28:15,173 --> 00:28:18,134
The most famous martyr
besides independence fighters

536
00:28:18,218 --> 00:28:19,302
is the Heating Bill Martyr.

537
00:28:20,845 --> 00:28:22,805
Heating Bill Martyr…

538
00:28:30,563 --> 00:28:33,650
PARK HAE-KANG IS HERE
TO PROTECT YOUR HEATING BILL!

539
00:28:33,733 --> 00:28:35,777
TAKE RESPONSIBILITY
FOR HEATING BILL CORRUPTION!

540
00:28:48,373 --> 00:28:51,209
They're going totally overboard.

541
00:28:54,087 --> 00:28:56,714
Everyone, what kind of people are we?

542
00:28:57,507 --> 00:28:59,926
We are a resilient people
who roamed the Manchurian Plains,

543
00:29:00,009 --> 00:29:02,095
spread our gallantry across the world

544
00:29:02,178 --> 00:29:05,849
and stood united
against foreign invasions and crises.

545
00:29:05,932 --> 00:29:09,477
I am standing here now with the spirit
of the independence fighters

546
00:29:09,561 --> 00:29:12,188
who gave everything to resist
during our nation's biggest crisis.

547
00:29:12,272 --> 00:29:13,356
Everyone.

548
00:29:13,439 --> 00:29:16,317
A total of 123 households

549
00:29:16,401 --> 00:29:20,989
have not paid any heating bills
for six whole years.

550
00:29:21,072 --> 00:29:22,657
I discovered this fact!

551
00:29:23,616 --> 00:29:26,327
Those 123 households
have been enjoying free heating

552
00:29:26,411 --> 00:29:29,038
thanks to someone's abuse of power.

553
00:29:29,122 --> 00:29:31,332
Zero heating bills?

554
00:29:31,416 --> 00:29:33,084
Yes, Ms. Senior Secretary.

555
00:29:33,167 --> 00:29:36,963
I could not remain silent
in the face of such abuse of power.

556
00:29:37,046 --> 00:29:39,257
I promise to expose
all the hidden corruption

557
00:29:39,340 --> 00:29:40,925
within this apartment complex

558
00:29:41,509 --> 00:29:43,261
and fight…

559
00:29:45,054 --> 00:29:46,598
against these illegal acts!

560
00:29:48,516 --> 00:29:49,559
Everyone!

561
00:29:49,642 --> 00:29:51,728
Heating Bill Martyr!

562
00:29:53,438 --> 00:29:55,148
Problem-solver Park Hae-kang!

563
00:29:57,692 --> 00:29:59,485
Heating Bill Martyr!

564
00:30:01,154 --> 00:30:02,780
Problem-solver Park Hae-kang!

565
00:30:02,864 --> 00:30:04,157
Pay your heating bills!

566
00:30:04,240 --> 00:30:06,784
We should all pay our heating bills!

567
00:30:10,872 --> 00:30:12,707
I will solve this problem, everyone.

568
00:30:13,333 --> 00:30:16,628
The former president and building reps
weren't paying their heating bills.

569
00:30:16,711 --> 00:30:18,630
Shouldn't we catch those thieves first?

570
00:30:18,713 --> 00:30:20,632
Those jerks took our money.

571
00:30:20,715 --> 00:30:23,718
All the other households
were paying for their heating bills.

572
00:30:23,801 --> 00:30:25,053
This is so unfair.

573
00:30:25,136 --> 00:30:26,804
This isn't mismanagement. It's fraud.

574
00:30:26,888 --> 00:30:29,265
Did we elect these people
as representatives

575
00:30:29,349 --> 00:30:31,267
just so they could rip us off?

576
00:30:31,351 --> 00:30:33,686
Don't make excuses. Take responsibility.

577
00:30:33,770 --> 00:30:36,272
We will not let this slide.

578
00:30:37,315 --> 00:30:38,191
Wait.

579
00:30:39,108 --> 00:30:41,069
I was a mathematics major.

580
00:30:41,653 --> 00:30:44,697
Let's say the average heating bill
for a 112-square-meter house in winter

581
00:30:44,781 --> 00:30:45,949
is about 200,000 won.

582
00:30:46,032 --> 00:30:48,910
Then it'll be one million
over five months,

583
00:30:48,993 --> 00:30:50,620
and six million over six years.

584
00:30:50,703 --> 00:30:53,665
There's also hot water usage
for spring, summer, and fall.

585
00:30:53,748 --> 00:30:55,833
Then let's say it's about
ten million in total.

586
00:30:55,917 --> 00:30:58,002
But there are 123 households,

587
00:30:58,086 --> 00:30:59,629
so it's 1.23 billion.

588
00:31:00,463 --> 00:31:02,840
1.23 billion?

589
00:31:05,426 --> 00:31:09,931
This shall be known as the "123 Incident."

590
00:31:15,770 --> 00:31:17,355
We weren't aware of this.

591
00:31:17,438 --> 00:31:19,524
We'll be checking all 123 households.

592
00:31:19,607 --> 00:31:22,068
We can't check all the bills
for each household every month.

593
00:31:22,151 --> 00:31:23,945
Don't worry. Please just wait…

594
00:31:24,028 --> 00:31:25,488
Yes, I'm sorry.

595
00:31:25,571 --> 00:31:26,864
We sincerely apologize.

596
00:31:26,948 --> 00:31:28,241
All right.

597
00:31:32,120 --> 00:31:33,413
We had no idea.

598
00:31:33,496 --> 00:31:35,540
You have to play dumb, no matter what.

599
00:31:42,672 --> 00:31:44,173
This is the management office.

600
00:31:44,257 --> 00:31:45,591
What do we do now?

601
00:31:45,675 --> 00:31:48,052
Park Hae-kang just had to meddle again.

602
00:31:48,136 --> 00:31:51,723
It seems like
he's doing everything he can to annoy us.

603
00:31:52,724 --> 00:31:55,810
We should've stopped him
from getting elected, no matter what.

604
00:31:55,893 --> 00:31:56,769
You're right.

605
00:31:56,853 --> 00:32:00,356
What do we do?
The online forum is in an uproar.

606
00:32:01,315 --> 00:32:06,279
Sir, please say something.

607
00:32:09,323 --> 00:32:10,450
Well…

608
00:32:13,202 --> 00:32:15,329
just insist that we didn't know…

609
00:32:16,581 --> 00:32:18,166
the gas meter was broken.

610
00:32:18,249 --> 00:32:21,085
What can they do if we say we didn't know?

611
00:32:23,171 --> 00:32:26,257
Would that work, though?

612
00:32:27,091 --> 00:32:30,219
Then should we just admit
that the building reps

613
00:32:30,303 --> 00:32:33,389
and some residents
who wrote comments for us

614
00:32:33,473 --> 00:32:35,391
received zero heating bills until now?

615
00:32:35,475 --> 00:32:36,893
Should I just tell the truth?

616
00:32:36,976 --> 00:32:38,519
Should we all go down together?

617
00:32:38,603 --> 00:32:41,898
You've been enjoying the benefits
for a long time.

618
00:32:41,981 --> 00:32:44,108
Use your brains…

619
00:32:45,026 --> 00:32:47,612
to think, will you?

620
00:32:47,695 --> 00:32:49,655
Just use your brains.

621
00:32:49,739 --> 00:32:51,491
Can't you think?

622
00:32:52,241 --> 00:32:56,621
Your penthouse also had zero heating bills
for the past six years.

623
00:32:57,246 --> 00:33:00,458
It seems President Seo
was overly loyal to you.

624
00:33:00,541 --> 00:33:04,253
It looks like Seo Gang-won
was busy doing something interesting.

625
00:33:04,337 --> 00:33:05,713
The other 122 households

626
00:33:05,797 --> 00:33:07,590
were close to President Seo

627
00:33:07,673 --> 00:33:09,300
or had some kind of connection.

628
00:33:11,010 --> 00:33:13,387
Gang-won is quite bold, isn't he?

629
00:33:13,471 --> 00:33:16,099
He did something
I didn't even tell him to do.

630
00:33:17,183 --> 00:33:19,018
What on earth was he thinking?

631
00:33:20,144 --> 00:33:21,312
Excuse me, sir.

632
00:33:22,688 --> 00:33:24,190
LEE SANG-GYU, GONGYEONG DAILY PRESIDENT

633
00:33:25,525 --> 00:33:28,486
-I think you should take this, sir.
-All right.

634
00:33:30,071 --> 00:33:32,073
Hello. How have you been?

635
00:33:32,156 --> 00:33:34,408
I was about to give you a call.

636
00:33:35,660 --> 00:33:37,745
You're low on fuel, aren't you?

637
00:33:38,454 --> 00:33:40,540
Why don't we fill it up?

638
00:33:43,334 --> 00:33:44,252
Mr. Kim.

639
00:33:44,335 --> 00:33:46,671
Let's use the reserve fund.

640
00:33:50,216 --> 00:33:52,760
"Relics discovered at Oman New Town site…

641
00:33:53,469 --> 00:33:55,054
found to be fabricated.

642
00:33:56,556 --> 00:33:59,976
Planned by a group
opposing the new town project."

643
00:34:01,102 --> 00:34:02,395
Isn't that a nice scenario?

644
00:34:03,729 --> 00:34:05,898
Give him a full tank.

645
00:34:06,899 --> 00:34:08,526
A sedan for Gongyeong Daily…

646
00:34:10,069 --> 00:34:11,946
and a fruit box for the online media.

647
00:34:13,948 --> 00:34:15,908
The dream of owning a home
has been delayed again.

648
00:34:15,992 --> 00:34:19,287
YouTubers have a large influence
on public opinion these days,

649
00:34:19,370 --> 00:34:20,872
so let's grease some palms there too.

650
00:34:20,955 --> 00:34:23,583
How will they fill
the housing supply target of 70,000 units?

651
00:34:23,666 --> 00:34:25,042
Send something sweet.

652
00:34:25,126 --> 00:34:28,838
So why? Who is trying
to stop the new town project?

653
00:34:28,921 --> 00:34:30,590
Planting relics at the site?

654
00:34:32,300 --> 00:34:33,926
Mr. Kim.

655
00:34:34,010 --> 00:34:37,180
We spent a huge sum today, haven't we?

656
00:34:37,263 --> 00:34:40,141
I'm sure the media will move
after using all that money.

657
00:34:40,975 --> 00:34:44,478
And you spent three billion
on Hyeonpo Apartment last year,

658
00:34:44,562 --> 00:34:45,771
but there's an audit soon.

659
00:34:45,855 --> 00:34:46,814
What will you do?

660
00:34:48,858 --> 00:34:50,693
The apartment complex in Soyeong-dong.

661
00:34:50,776 --> 00:34:52,904
How much is left in that reserve fund?

662
00:34:52,987 --> 00:34:55,990
We're using that fund too,

663
00:34:56,073 --> 00:34:58,534
so there's a little over six billion left.

664
00:34:59,535 --> 00:35:01,204
I should use that then.

665
00:35:04,957 --> 00:35:06,209
You know,

666
00:35:06,918 --> 00:35:09,795
whenever I use the reserve fund
from an apartment complex,

667
00:35:11,214 --> 00:35:15,009
I feel like a kid raiding a piggy bank
without telling Dad.

668
00:35:16,010 --> 00:35:17,720
But Dad doesn't have a clue.

669
00:35:17,803 --> 00:35:19,680
Just like the residents.

670
00:35:23,226 --> 00:35:26,646
What excuse will they come up with
for not paying the heating bill?

671
00:35:26,729 --> 00:35:27,813
It's obvious.

672
00:35:27,897 --> 00:35:29,857
They'll say the gas meter was broken,

673
00:35:29,941 --> 00:35:31,317
but they had no clue.

674
00:35:31,400 --> 00:35:33,527
It's always the same excuse.

675
00:35:33,611 --> 00:35:35,238
It doesn't matter what they say.

676
00:35:35,321 --> 00:35:38,616
We just have to check
if the reserve fund is being disbursed.

677
00:35:38,699 --> 00:35:42,453
You're sure gas meter replacements
are done with the reserve fund?

678
00:35:42,536 --> 00:35:44,747
Yes. It's different
for every apartment complex,

679
00:35:44,830 --> 00:35:46,874
but, fortunately,
it's stated in the regulations.

680
00:35:46,958 --> 00:35:49,126
-You'd better be sure.
-I am.

681
00:35:49,710 --> 00:35:52,964
And we can use this chance to wipe out

682
00:35:53,631 --> 00:35:56,634
President Seo's faction in one go.

683
00:36:01,722 --> 00:36:03,557
TRUE VALUE STATE
123 INCIDENT HEARING

684
00:36:03,641 --> 00:36:05,393
Do you think we're running a charity?

685
00:36:05,476 --> 00:36:06,894
This should be front-page news!

686
00:36:06,978 --> 00:36:09,105
I just can't believe this!

687
00:36:09,981 --> 00:36:11,774
How could you do this to all of us?

688
00:36:15,069 --> 00:36:16,696
I will step down

689
00:36:17,280 --> 00:36:19,448
and return to being an ordinary resident

690
00:36:19,532 --> 00:36:21,367
of True Value--

691
00:36:21,450 --> 00:36:23,160
Are you kidding me?

692
00:36:23,244 --> 00:36:25,913
Stepping down won't solve anything!

693
00:36:25,997 --> 00:36:28,416
You think that will make it okay?

694
00:36:28,499 --> 00:36:32,253
We need to report this to the police.

695
00:36:32,837 --> 00:36:34,839
We need to request an audit

696
00:36:34,922 --> 00:36:38,217
and figure out exactly what happened,

697
00:36:38,301 --> 00:36:41,012
down to every last detail.

698
00:36:41,095 --> 00:36:41,929
Don't you agree?

699
00:36:42,013 --> 00:36:43,848
-You're right!
-Yes!

700
00:36:45,391 --> 00:36:46,642
I mean…

701
00:36:46,726 --> 00:36:50,187
Honestly, I don't get
why you're blaming everything on us.

702
00:36:50,271 --> 00:36:52,064
Our gas meters were broken.

703
00:36:52,148 --> 00:36:54,191
What were we supposed to do?

704
00:36:54,275 --> 00:36:57,611
Do you all just stare
at your gas meters every day?

705
00:36:58,612 --> 00:37:01,324
Even if you didn't see your gas meter,

706
00:37:01,407 --> 00:37:03,826
you would've seen your bill.

707
00:37:03,909 --> 00:37:07,079
You had zero heating bills
in the middle of winter.

708
00:37:07,163 --> 00:37:10,082
How could you not know
for six whole years?

709
00:37:10,166 --> 00:37:11,584
Six years!

710
00:37:12,209 --> 00:37:15,296
Do you hear what he's saying?
He's supposed to be a building rep!

711
00:37:15,379 --> 00:37:18,549
-Ridiculous.
-Building reps are people too!

712
00:37:18,632 --> 00:37:21,969
Sometimes we're too busy
to check our bills.

713
00:37:22,053 --> 00:37:24,847
I set up automatic payments,
so I don't check them sometimes.

714
00:37:24,930 --> 00:37:25,848
Automatic payments?

715
00:37:25,931 --> 00:37:27,433
Are we not people too?

716
00:37:27,516 --> 00:37:29,894
Are you kidding me? "Automatic payments"?

717
00:37:29,977 --> 00:37:31,812
This is just nonsense. Hey.

718
00:37:31,896 --> 00:37:35,358
Even so, this is strange.

719
00:37:35,441 --> 00:37:39,653
Why did this happen
only to the building representatives?

720
00:37:39,737 --> 00:37:41,739
That's exactly what I mean.

721
00:37:41,822 --> 00:37:45,368
And we mothers really can't understand
how the facility manager

722
00:37:45,451 --> 00:37:47,495
didn't know about this for six years.

723
00:37:47,578 --> 00:37:49,914
It's your job to oversee this, Mr. Choi.

724
00:37:49,997 --> 00:37:51,916
Mr. Choi, come over here.

725
00:37:51,999 --> 00:37:53,918
Say something. Come over here.

726
00:37:54,001 --> 00:37:57,338
-Tell us.
-Just tell us everything.

727
00:37:57,421 --> 00:37:58,672
What happened?

728
00:37:58,756 --> 00:38:00,716
Just explain everything.

729
00:38:03,928 --> 00:38:05,763
I…

730
00:38:10,226 --> 00:38:11,060
Well…

731
00:38:11,143 --> 00:38:12,645
This is infuriating.

732
00:38:13,396 --> 00:38:16,023
I have nothing to say.

733
00:38:16,107 --> 00:38:17,483
I'm really sorry.

734
00:38:19,235 --> 00:38:21,904
Mr. Choi, I'm disappointed in you.

735
00:38:21,987 --> 00:38:23,656
I had no idea he was that kind of person.

736
00:38:23,739 --> 00:38:24,615
Unbelievable.

737
00:38:25,991 --> 00:38:28,202
Calm down, everyone!

738
00:38:28,285 --> 00:38:30,037
I understand how you feel,

739
00:38:30,121 --> 00:38:34,041
but this has already happened,
so we must figure out how to resolve this.

740
00:38:34,125 --> 00:38:36,127
The most urgent matter

741
00:38:36,210 --> 00:38:38,629
is to replace the broken gas meters.

742
00:38:39,296 --> 00:38:40,923
-With the reserve fund--
-But…

743
00:38:41,006 --> 00:38:41,882
Yes?

744
00:38:41,966 --> 00:38:44,093
Why would you use
the reserve fund for that?

745
00:38:45,845 --> 00:38:47,346
The management regulations

746
00:38:47,430 --> 00:38:50,766
state that gas meter replacements
should be done with the reserve fund.

747
00:38:50,850 --> 00:38:54,562
So I'll take care of that issue
according to the regulations.

748
00:38:56,397 --> 00:38:58,399
Is there something you'd like to say?

749
00:39:00,860 --> 00:39:04,155
I live on the top floor of Building 123.

750
00:39:04,238 --> 00:39:07,491
It turns out that
I had zero heating bills as well.

751
00:39:08,284 --> 00:39:09,702
I wasn't aware.

752
00:39:09,785 --> 00:39:14,290
I don't check the gas meter or my bills.

753
00:39:14,373 --> 00:39:18,294
I know it may sound irresponsible
to say I didn't know,

754
00:39:19,044 --> 00:39:22,506
but I agree with
what the building reps are saying.

755
00:39:25,759 --> 00:39:28,554
There was something going on with him too.

756
00:39:28,637 --> 00:39:29,847
That is why

757
00:39:30,431 --> 00:39:32,349
I will pay for all the heating bills

758
00:39:32,433 --> 00:39:34,935
I haven't paid for until now.

759
00:39:36,103 --> 00:39:38,564
Wouldn't it only be right
for all the building reps

760
00:39:39,148 --> 00:39:40,524
to do the same?

761
00:39:41,150 --> 00:39:42,234
Wait.

762
00:39:42,318 --> 00:39:44,820
This wasn't our fault.

763
00:39:44,904 --> 00:39:46,947
Why should we pay for everything--

764
00:39:47,031 --> 00:39:49,783
Well, you've found out now,
so you should pay your bills.

765
00:39:50,367 --> 00:39:52,161
The heating bills that you haven't paid

766
00:39:52,244 --> 00:39:55,331
have been paid
by all the other residents so far.

767
00:39:55,915 --> 00:39:59,168
You should at least be feeling sorry.

768
00:39:59,251 --> 00:40:00,544
We're all neighbors.

769
00:40:00,628 --> 00:40:02,671
-He's right.
-Right.

770
00:40:02,755 --> 00:40:03,589
Everyone.

771
00:40:03,672 --> 00:40:06,383
The man living in the penthouse
really is different.

772
00:40:06,467 --> 00:40:09,094
They say generosity comes from money,

773
00:40:09,178 --> 00:40:11,430
but he also seems to have a conscience.

774
00:40:11,514 --> 00:40:13,224
That's very admirable.

775
00:40:14,808 --> 00:40:15,935
You're so cool.

776
00:40:16,018 --> 00:40:17,561
-You're cool!
-Very admirable.

777
00:40:21,190 --> 00:40:22,233
Mr. Seo.

778
00:40:25,110 --> 00:40:26,487
What do you think?

779
00:40:28,864 --> 00:40:30,324
Me? I…

780
00:40:31,617 --> 00:40:32,576
Mr. Seo.

781
00:40:41,293 --> 00:40:42,461
Well, I…

782
00:40:43,504 --> 00:40:45,381
Since you asked for my opinion,

783
00:40:45,464 --> 00:40:49,426
I also believe we should pay
for all the heating bills.

784
00:40:49,510 --> 00:40:51,262
-President Seo.
-President Seo.

785
00:40:51,345 --> 00:40:52,846
What are you saying?

786
00:40:54,932 --> 00:40:56,016
Of course.

787
00:40:56,100 --> 00:40:58,143
Of course, they should pay their bills.

788
00:40:58,644 --> 00:41:00,479
All right. That's great.

789
00:41:00,980 --> 00:41:02,231
Then now,

790
00:41:02,773 --> 00:41:05,276
I'll recheck all the households
that had zero heating bills

791
00:41:05,359 --> 00:41:07,903
and collect all the fees
that they haven't paid.

792
00:41:07,987 --> 00:41:10,072
And I'll make sure

793
00:41:10,155 --> 00:41:13,826
to distribute the collected fees
to the remaining 9,677 households

794
00:41:13,909 --> 00:41:16,704
who have had to pay extra until now.

795
00:41:18,205 --> 00:41:19,290
You're amazing!

796
00:41:19,373 --> 00:41:20,457
We love you!

797
00:41:32,636 --> 00:41:33,929
President Park.

798
00:41:41,645 --> 00:41:44,440
You seemed as wise as King Solomon today.

799
00:41:44,523 --> 00:41:46,567
"Recover the unjust gains

800
00:41:46,650 --> 00:41:49,820
and distribute them equally
to the people."

801
00:41:51,614 --> 00:41:53,282
That was so cool.

802
00:41:53,365 --> 00:41:55,618
I was more impressed by your words.

803
00:41:55,701 --> 00:41:57,161
In any case, thank you.

804
00:41:57,745 --> 00:42:00,372
Keep up the good work, President Park.

805
00:42:03,542 --> 00:42:04,418
Bye.

806
00:42:04,501 --> 00:42:06,337
-Thank you.
-Bye.

807
00:42:06,420 --> 00:42:08,714
I was curious what kind of people
lived in penthouses.

808
00:42:08,797 --> 00:42:09,798
Mr. Lee?

809
00:42:09,882 --> 00:42:12,593
He's very humble and cool,
unlike many rich people.

810
00:42:12,676 --> 00:42:14,386
-You know him?
-When did you start admiring him?

811
00:42:14,470 --> 00:42:15,596
Since the moment we saw him.

812
00:42:15,679 --> 00:42:17,348
Anyone rich is admirable.

813
00:42:17,431 --> 00:42:19,767
Great job, President Park.

814
00:42:19,850 --> 00:42:21,685
-Thank you.
-We're rooting for you.

815
00:42:21,769 --> 00:42:22,603
Thank you.

816
00:42:22,686 --> 00:42:24,813
Goodbye.

817
00:42:28,942 --> 00:42:31,654
You did a decent job today.

818
00:42:32,237 --> 00:42:33,364
But…

819
00:42:34,073 --> 00:42:36,075
don't let your guard down.

820
00:42:36,158 --> 00:42:39,995
I'm keeping an eye on you.

821
00:42:41,914 --> 00:42:44,208
Good job today, guys. See you later.

822
00:42:44,291 --> 00:42:45,793
-Bye.
-Bye, Ms. Senior Secretary.

823
00:42:45,876 --> 00:42:47,002
Get home safely, ma'am.

824
00:42:47,586 --> 00:42:49,088
You should lose some weight.

825
00:42:50,422 --> 00:42:51,256
Mr. Kim.

826
00:42:51,924 --> 00:42:53,717
Have you seen Spider-Man?

827
00:42:54,593 --> 00:42:56,970
Yes, a long time ago.

828
00:43:02,393 --> 00:43:05,145
"With great power
comes great responsibility."

829
00:43:05,229 --> 00:43:06,146
The famous quote?

830
00:43:06,939 --> 00:43:08,607
Yes.

831
00:43:09,149 --> 00:43:11,402
It's time for Seo Gang-won

832
00:43:11,485 --> 00:43:13,862
to take responsibility.

833
00:43:14,363 --> 00:43:17,616
I gave him power over 9,800 households,

834
00:43:18,450 --> 00:43:21,161
but he gave birth
to a heating bill martyr.

835
00:43:22,705 --> 00:43:25,499
Will you invite Gang-won
on a date with me?

836
00:43:26,500 --> 00:43:27,334
Yes, sir.

837
00:43:33,966 --> 00:43:35,426
Were you all notified?

838
00:43:35,926 --> 00:43:37,720
-About the 123 Incident heating bills?
-Yes.

839
00:43:38,303 --> 00:43:41,849
We'll each get an equal share
of the fees paid by the 123 households.

840
00:43:42,933 --> 00:43:46,770
I heard they'll deduct that amount
from this month's maintenance fee.

841
00:43:46,854 --> 00:43:49,773
I should pay more attention
to my maintenance bill from now on.

842
00:43:49,857 --> 00:43:50,816
Me too.

843
00:43:50,899 --> 00:43:53,777
I never paid attention
since it's paid from my husband's account.

844
00:43:54,278 --> 00:43:55,362
In any case,

845
00:43:55,904 --> 00:43:58,699
isn't our president
really good at his job?

846
00:43:58,782 --> 00:44:00,576
He's handsome, and he's so capable.

847
00:44:00,659 --> 00:44:01,493
I know, right?

848
00:44:01,577 --> 00:44:04,913
These days, I've been watching
all the residents' association meetings.

849
00:44:04,997 --> 00:44:06,498
It's like I'm watching a celebrity.

850
00:44:07,499 --> 00:44:09,626
He does seem a bit different.

851
00:44:09,710 --> 00:44:13,213
I can sense his passion.

852
00:44:13,297 --> 00:44:16,508
What he did regarding the heating bills
was pretty touching.

853
00:44:16,592 --> 00:44:21,513
The way he exposed the 123 Incident
and even resolved the issue…

854
00:44:22,014 --> 00:44:24,683
I feel so relieved
that our residents' association president

855
00:44:24,767 --> 00:44:25,976
is someone like him.

856
00:44:26,560 --> 00:44:28,270
-True.
-You're right.

857
00:44:28,353 --> 00:44:30,105
Totally. I'm so happy.

858
00:44:30,189 --> 00:44:31,523
Yes!

859
00:44:31,607 --> 00:44:33,066
Let's have beer next time.

860
00:44:33,150 --> 00:44:34,568
How about some beer?

861
00:44:38,614 --> 00:44:41,074
PRESIDENT PARK HAE-KANG

862
00:44:46,955 --> 00:44:47,790
Yes?

863
00:44:53,170 --> 00:44:54,922
You're here, Ms. Senior Secretary.

864
00:44:57,382 --> 00:44:58,634
Come and sit down.

865
00:45:12,648 --> 00:45:15,442
You said you needed a week.

866
00:45:15,526 --> 00:45:16,735
Was that…

867
00:45:17,361 --> 00:45:20,322
so you could take care
of the 123 Incident?

868
00:45:21,823 --> 00:45:23,575
It was an urgent matter.

869
00:45:31,291 --> 00:45:34,461
I already have so much to do.

870
00:45:35,128 --> 00:45:37,214
That you do.

871
00:45:38,340 --> 00:45:39,174
But…

872
00:45:40,175 --> 00:45:42,636
would a week be enough, President Park?

873
00:45:43,971 --> 00:45:44,805
What?

874
00:45:48,517 --> 00:45:50,143
Goodbye, Ms. Senior Secretary.

875
00:46:04,157 --> 00:46:07,828
With great power
comes great responsibility.

876
00:46:10,706 --> 00:46:11,790
Sir.

877
00:46:16,086 --> 00:46:16,920
Yes?

878
00:46:17,754 --> 00:46:19,423
It's me, sir.

879
00:46:19,506 --> 00:46:23,010
I know you must be busy,

880
00:46:23,635 --> 00:46:26,555
but I wanted to ask
when I should come pick up the money.

881
00:46:27,556 --> 00:46:29,558
Come in two hours.

882
00:46:30,142 --> 00:46:30,976
All right.

883
00:46:48,035 --> 00:46:50,245
This is premium Italian hardwood flooring.

884
00:46:51,455 --> 00:46:53,582
They said it was resistant to cracking.

885
00:46:54,541 --> 00:46:56,251
Mr. Kim, I think it's cracked.

886
00:46:58,378 --> 00:47:01,632
It seems like you hit the floor
a little too hard with the golf club.

887
00:47:01,715 --> 00:47:03,634
But it doesn't really show.

888
00:47:06,094 --> 00:47:07,262
Really?

889
00:47:09,389 --> 00:47:10,974
Damn it.

890
00:47:12,726 --> 00:47:17,564
My 300-million-won floor
almost got ruined because of you.

891
00:47:18,190 --> 00:47:19,274
Can't you hear me?

892
00:47:22,986 --> 00:47:23,820
Seo Gang-won.

893
00:47:24,446 --> 00:47:25,280
Seo Gang-won.

894
00:47:25,864 --> 00:47:27,824
Wake up, Seo Gang-won!

895
00:47:27,908 --> 00:47:31,203
Seo Gang-won!

896
00:47:36,500 --> 00:47:38,418
You can't just die like this.

897
00:47:40,212 --> 00:47:42,130
Don't you know how much I lost?

898
00:47:42,214 --> 00:47:44,508
You should've served your purpose
until the end.

899
00:47:45,717 --> 00:47:47,469
-Mr. Kim.
-Yes, sir.

900
00:47:48,387 --> 00:47:50,097
We should move him

901
00:47:51,139 --> 00:47:53,183
to Taegowon.

902
00:48:01,024 --> 00:48:02,150
Be careful.

903
00:48:12,911 --> 00:48:14,788
TAEGOWON

904
00:48:18,625 --> 00:48:20,252
All right!

905
00:48:32,639 --> 00:48:34,057
Thinking back on it,

906
00:48:34,141 --> 00:48:37,394
you really didn't have anything to offer.

907
00:48:38,103 --> 00:48:40,856
You weren't capable,
and you weren't even funny either.

908
00:48:41,440 --> 00:48:43,275
So why don't you

909
00:48:43,358 --> 00:48:45,235
become fertilizer for this mountain…

910
00:48:46,570 --> 00:48:49,406
and take good care…

911
00:48:51,032 --> 00:48:52,325
of our baby trees now?

912
00:49:03,920 --> 00:49:05,589
Take good care of them.

913
00:49:27,235 --> 00:49:30,238
Where the hell is he going?

914
00:49:31,072 --> 00:49:32,532
Something's fishy.

915
00:49:57,015 --> 00:49:58,016
He's going inside.

916
00:50:13,907 --> 00:50:15,325
-Did you take it?
-Yes.

917
00:50:19,162 --> 00:50:21,081
"Tae…" What is it?

918
00:50:21,665 --> 00:50:22,749
"Taegowon."

919
00:50:22,833 --> 00:50:24,209
-Taegowon?
-Yes.

920
00:50:24,292 --> 00:50:25,710
What is this place?

921
00:50:34,719 --> 00:50:37,973
SEO GANG-WON

922
00:50:39,975 --> 00:50:41,101
Hello.

923
00:50:42,185 --> 00:50:44,145
You arrived just in time.

924
00:50:44,229 --> 00:50:45,063
Yes, sir.

925
00:50:45,689 --> 00:50:47,816
-Mr. Kim, give him the money.
-Yes, sir.

926
00:50:54,197 --> 00:50:55,615
I don't get

927
00:50:56,324 --> 00:50:57,659
how Park Hae-kang found out.

928
00:50:58,493 --> 00:51:00,203
-I'm sorry, sir.
-No, it's fine.

929
00:51:00,829 --> 00:51:02,455
It was quite amusing.

930
00:51:02,539 --> 00:51:05,166
I swear I won't let it happen again--

931
00:51:05,250 --> 00:51:06,459
Don't.

932
00:51:07,794 --> 00:51:08,628
Pardon?

933
00:51:09,629 --> 00:51:11,006
I'm enjoying this,

934
00:51:12,173 --> 00:51:14,718
so just let Park Hae-kang
do what he wants.

935
00:51:16,636 --> 00:51:18,096
Yes, sir.

936
00:51:19,514 --> 00:51:22,809
Since you're here,
you should pay your respects.

937
00:51:25,020 --> 00:51:25,896
All right.

938
00:51:27,147 --> 00:51:28,189
Here.

939
00:51:33,486 --> 00:51:35,488
Former President Seo Gang-won's…

940
00:51:36,865 --> 00:51:37,866
tree.

941
00:51:40,076 --> 00:51:44,456
This is the tree that will grow
with Seo Gang-won's flesh and blood.

942
00:51:48,293 --> 00:51:50,587
Let's pay our respects.

943
00:51:53,298 --> 00:51:55,216
May you live a long life.

944
00:52:14,027 --> 00:52:14,945
He's back.

945
00:52:15,028 --> 00:52:16,321
Take photos.

946
00:52:20,742 --> 00:52:21,826
That's a bag of cash.

947
00:52:22,661 --> 00:52:23,745
Cash?

948
00:52:30,585 --> 00:52:31,544
Taegowon?

949
00:52:31,628 --> 00:52:33,505
The facility manager tripped,

950
00:52:33,588 --> 00:52:36,466
and that bag was filled
with 50,000 won bills.

951
00:52:36,967 --> 00:52:39,135
Did any other employees
do anything suspicious?

952
00:52:39,219 --> 00:52:42,263
Besides the facility manager,
everyone else is working late.

953
00:52:42,347 --> 00:52:44,432
And they're replacing
the gas meters tomorrow?

954
00:52:44,516 --> 00:52:45,892
Yes, sir.

955
00:52:45,976 --> 00:52:48,895
Then the facility manager
must have gotten the money for that.

956
00:52:49,479 --> 00:52:51,606
I did a search,
and Taegowon is a tree farm.

957
00:52:51,690 --> 00:52:54,359
They mostly sell trees
used for apartment landscaping.

958
00:52:55,402 --> 00:52:57,112
A tree farm?

959
00:53:04,828 --> 00:53:06,663
TAESAN PARK
TAESAN CONSTRUCTION, TAESAN PLANT…

960
00:53:08,164 --> 00:53:09,499
TS NETWORKS

961
00:53:09,582 --> 00:53:11,626
Taegowon is owned by TS Networks.

962
00:53:11,710 --> 00:53:13,545
It's a real estate development company,

963
00:53:13,628 --> 00:53:15,714
one of Taesan Construction's affiliates.

964
00:53:15,797 --> 00:53:17,173
And TS Networks

965
00:53:17,257 --> 00:53:19,259
is True Value's developer,

966
00:53:19,342 --> 00:53:21,469
while Taesan Construction
is the construction company.

967
00:53:21,553 --> 00:53:22,887
TAESAN CONSTRUCTION

968
00:53:22,971 --> 00:53:25,765
That means Taesan is behind all this.

969
00:53:26,349 --> 00:53:27,517
Would they even see us?

970
00:53:31,187 --> 00:53:32,022
Boss.

971
00:53:32,105 --> 00:53:32,939
Huh?

972
00:53:33,023 --> 00:53:35,483
Places like this won't see you
without an appointment.

973
00:53:36,359 --> 00:53:37,402
Just let me give it a try.

974
00:53:40,530 --> 00:53:41,448
Hello.

975
00:53:42,907 --> 00:53:44,743
Please inform the president
that True Value's

976
00:53:44,826 --> 00:53:47,245
residents' association president
is here to see them.

977
00:53:47,328 --> 00:53:48,788
He's waiting for you, sir.

978
00:53:49,372 --> 00:53:51,166
-What?
-Please follow me.

979
00:53:53,001 --> 00:53:54,377
It wasn't me.

980
00:54:01,426 --> 00:54:05,430
…46, 47, 48, 49, 50, 51, 52.

981
00:54:05,513 --> 00:54:07,140
That's 52 points,

982
00:54:07,223 --> 00:54:09,934
with pibak, gwangbak, meongtta,

983
00:54:10,018 --> 00:54:11,686
a shake, a three-go and a four-go,

984
00:54:11,770 --> 00:54:13,646
so it'll be 342,800 won.

985
00:54:15,648 --> 00:54:19,194
If someone's winning over 300,000 won
in a 100-won-a-point game,

986
00:54:19,277 --> 00:54:21,404
it's no longer just a game.
That's gambling.

987
00:54:21,488 --> 00:54:23,490
Have you been visiting gambling dens?

988
00:54:24,282 --> 00:54:27,660
Go-Stop is all about momentum.

989
00:54:29,829 --> 00:54:30,955
Momentum.

990
00:54:31,039 --> 00:54:32,040
Come on.

991
00:54:32,749 --> 00:54:35,960
Even if we're a fake family,
I'm still your father-in-law.

992
00:54:36,461 --> 00:54:37,378
Ha-ri.

993
00:54:37,462 --> 00:54:39,547
At least give me a discount.

994
00:54:42,884 --> 00:54:44,719
Hang on. Hello?

995
00:54:44,803 --> 00:54:48,098
Hello, I'm Gyeong-buk's teacher
from the Stanford Class.

996
00:54:49,057 --> 00:54:51,935
Gyeong-buk seems to have a bit of a fever.

997
00:54:52,018 --> 00:54:54,354
What? Gyeong-buk has a fever?

998
00:54:55,563 --> 00:54:57,565
Please make sure everything goes smoothly.

999
00:54:57,649 --> 00:54:58,983
All right.

1000
00:55:00,235 --> 00:55:03,863
The gas meter replacements
will be done by today.

1001
00:55:04,781 --> 00:55:06,116
Great work, everyone.

1002
00:55:06,199 --> 00:55:08,451
We're not getting
any more calls from the residents.

1003
00:55:08,535 --> 00:55:10,453
We can finally get some rest.

1004
00:55:11,121 --> 00:55:13,706
Everyone's happy that
their maintenance fees will be reduced

1005
00:55:13,790 --> 00:55:15,375
with the recovered heating charges.

1006
00:55:15,458 --> 00:55:18,503
Why don't we have lunch together
to celebrate?

1007
00:55:18,586 --> 00:55:19,546
Yes!

1008
00:55:19,629 --> 00:55:22,465
We can recharge
and get our spirits back up.

1009
00:55:23,091 --> 00:55:25,301
Sure. Everyone worked hard.

1010
00:55:25,885 --> 00:55:27,762
It's lunchtime. Let's go.

1011
00:55:27,846 --> 00:55:29,973
-Yes, sir.
-Awesome.

1012
00:55:30,515 --> 00:55:32,183
Aren't you joining us, Ms. Kang?

1013
00:55:32,809 --> 00:55:34,269
I'm not feeling well.

1014
00:55:34,352 --> 00:55:35,937
Come with us, Ha-jeong.

1015
00:55:36,020 --> 00:55:37,897
You worked the hardest.

1016
00:55:37,981 --> 00:55:39,274
Come on.

1017
00:55:47,574 --> 00:55:49,033
-Come on, you scared me.
-Hey.

1018
00:55:49,868 --> 00:55:51,494
-Don't eat that.
-Sorry.

1019
00:55:51,578 --> 00:55:54,497
Boss, she said
the president was waiting for us.

1020
00:55:54,581 --> 00:55:55,999
Isn't that strange?

1021
00:55:56,082 --> 00:55:57,917
Maybe we were being followed.

1022
00:55:58,001 --> 00:56:00,670
It feels like they set a trap,
knowing we were coming.

1023
00:56:06,342 --> 00:56:08,136
What took you so long, President Park?

1024
00:56:08,219 --> 00:56:10,638
I've been waiting for you all this time.

1025
00:56:12,974 --> 00:56:14,225
Come inside.

1026
00:56:14,309 --> 00:56:16,603
Let us talk, president to president.

1027
00:56:16,686 --> 00:56:19,355
Come on. Watch your step.

1028
00:56:19,439 --> 00:56:20,315
Boss…

1029
00:56:21,107 --> 00:56:24,569
PHARMACY

1030
00:56:25,195 --> 00:56:26,654
Are you sure you're okay?

1031
00:56:27,155 --> 00:56:28,031
Yes.

1032
00:56:28,656 --> 00:56:29,490
Let's go.

1033
00:56:30,867 --> 00:56:32,994
This isn't something to say
to a kindergartener,

1034
00:56:33,077 --> 00:56:35,246
but you should take care of your own body.

1035
00:56:35,330 --> 00:56:37,123
Being sick only hurts yourself.

1036
00:56:37,207 --> 00:56:40,460
No one can suffer in your place.
Not your dad or your uncles.

1037
00:56:40,543 --> 00:56:41,544
Okay.

1038
00:56:42,128 --> 00:56:43,254
Mom…

1039
00:56:43,338 --> 00:56:45,715
I mean, Ha-ri.

1040
00:56:47,175 --> 00:56:49,802
Can't you carry my bag today?

1041
00:56:51,221 --> 00:56:52,055
No.

1042
00:56:52,639 --> 00:56:55,892
People are meant to carry
the burdens assigned to them.

1043
00:56:55,975 --> 00:56:57,518
We all have to carry our own cross.

1044
00:56:57,602 --> 00:56:59,729
That's the weight of life.

1045
00:57:00,480 --> 00:57:02,649
My friends' moms

1046
00:57:02,732 --> 00:57:06,861
always carry their bags
as soon as they come pick them up.

1047
00:57:16,204 --> 00:57:17,580
There. Happy?

1048
00:57:18,206 --> 00:57:19,958
Ma'am.

1049
00:57:20,041 --> 00:57:21,834
-Hello.
-Hello.

1050
00:57:22,418 --> 00:57:23,378
Is someone sick?

1051
00:57:23,878 --> 00:57:25,964
Oh, your kid's sick.

1052
00:57:26,047 --> 00:57:27,382
-Oh, dear.
-Hello.

1053
00:57:27,465 --> 00:57:30,093
Do you have a fever?
I hope you get better soon.

1054
00:57:30,593 --> 00:57:34,514
Ma'am, President Park
didn't come to work today.

1055
00:57:34,597 --> 00:57:36,558
Do you know where he went?

1056
00:57:37,642 --> 00:57:39,811
-Well…
-Hello, ma'am.

1057
00:57:39,894 --> 00:57:41,980
-Hello.
-Hello.

1058
00:57:42,480 --> 00:57:43,731
-We'll get going.
-Sure.

1059
00:57:43,815 --> 00:57:45,149
-Bye.
-Bye.

1060
00:57:45,233 --> 00:57:46,901
-Get well soon.
-Bye.

1061
00:57:46,985 --> 00:57:47,986
Bye.

1062
00:58:00,707 --> 00:58:01,583
Ha-jeong.

1063
00:58:04,502 --> 00:58:07,046
This is my office. Come here.

1064
00:58:08,131 --> 00:58:09,507
You know,

1065
00:58:09,591 --> 00:58:12,468
I was so shocked by your performance.

1066
00:58:12,552 --> 00:58:14,596
I have so many questions.

1067
00:58:14,679 --> 00:58:17,223
How did you find out
about the heating bills?

1068
00:58:18,057 --> 00:58:19,767
Right. You found the relics too.

1069
00:58:19,851 --> 00:58:21,728
Are you just good at finding stuff?

1070
00:58:22,437 --> 00:58:24,188
But those relics were authentic.

1071
00:58:24,814 --> 00:58:26,608
Where did you get those from?

1072
00:58:27,191 --> 00:58:28,651
It must have cost a fortune.

1073
00:58:30,612 --> 00:58:31,487
Right.

1074
00:58:31,571 --> 00:58:34,532
I prepared a small gift for you, Mr. Park.

1075
00:58:34,616 --> 00:58:36,242
Do you want to see? Come on.

1076
00:58:37,535 --> 00:58:38,411
Here.

1077
00:58:39,579 --> 00:58:40,538
Come on.

1078
00:58:50,423 --> 00:58:51,382
Ta-da.

1079
00:58:53,009 --> 00:58:55,219
It was hard choosing which photo to frame

1080
00:58:55,303 --> 00:58:57,639
since you looked good
in every one of them.

1081
00:58:58,222 --> 00:58:59,182
Do you like it?

1082
00:59:01,351 --> 00:59:03,895
But I don't like it.

1083
00:59:03,978 --> 00:59:07,190
I should've gotten a clear shot
of the disappointed look on your face

1084
00:59:07,273 --> 00:59:10,193
when you heard the bank balance.

1085
00:59:11,527 --> 00:59:14,197
He knows everything.

1086
00:59:16,491 --> 00:59:17,325
Are you really…

1087
00:59:18,117 --> 00:59:19,994
the president of Taesan Construction?

1088
00:59:21,996 --> 00:59:22,955
Right.

1089
00:59:23,873 --> 00:59:25,667
I haven't introduced myself properly.

1090
00:59:27,669 --> 00:59:29,671
I'm the president of Taesan Construction,

1091
00:59:30,546 --> 00:59:31,756
Lee Chung-won.

1092
00:59:34,676 --> 00:59:37,136
I'm Lee Chung-won from Building 123.

1093
00:59:37,720 --> 00:59:38,638
We'll…

1094
00:59:40,765 --> 00:59:42,892
be seeing each other again.

1095
00:59:56,030 --> 00:59:58,282
You seem to be great at finding things,

1096
00:59:58,366 --> 01:00:00,660
so what are you looking for here
at Taesan Group?

1097
01:00:01,452 --> 01:00:04,539
Whatever it is, I'm afraid
you won't be able to find it here.

1098
01:00:05,123 --> 01:00:06,582
I feel sorry about that.

1099
01:00:08,543 --> 01:00:10,670
No, I've already found it.

1100
01:00:14,424 --> 01:00:15,341
Why don't you…

1101
01:00:16,926 --> 01:00:19,804
let me become your right-hand man?

1102
01:00:26,602 --> 01:00:29,522
THE APARTMENT JOB

1103
01:00:53,629 --> 01:00:56,966
I'll do whatever it takes to support you.

1104
01:00:57,049 --> 01:00:59,010
Ha-jeong, just go live your own life.

1105
01:00:59,093 --> 01:01:01,137
Ms. Kang, were you crying?

1106
01:01:01,220 --> 01:01:03,139
Mr. Park, please let me stay the night.

1107
01:01:03,723 --> 01:01:05,349
A love story?

1108
01:01:05,433 --> 01:01:07,727
President Seo was the keeper of my vault.

1109
01:01:07,810 --> 01:01:10,146
I'm going to become
Lee Chung-won's vault keeper.

1110
01:01:10,229 --> 01:01:12,356
-Let's go meet President Seo first.
-President Seo?

1111
01:01:12,440 --> 01:01:14,692
-He went on a trip abroad?
-I don't know.

1112
01:01:14,776 --> 01:01:16,027
He betrayed us.

1113
01:01:16,110 --> 01:01:18,362
Release Yong-man on medical bail first.

1114
01:01:18,446 --> 01:01:19,989
Bring the cash, then we'll talk.

1115
01:01:20,072 --> 01:01:22,867
It seems Chief Son
is holding Park Yong-man hostage.

1116
01:01:22,950 --> 01:01:25,328
So that's why Park Hae-kang
needed the money.

1117
01:01:25,411 --> 01:01:27,830
Boss, becoming Lee Chung-won's
vault keeper is dangerous.

1118
01:01:27,914 --> 01:01:29,290
Do you trust Park Hae-kang?

1119
01:01:29,373 --> 01:01:32,710
I'm going to put him to the test.

1120
01:01:36,839 --> 01:01:38,841
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park

